# Atomic Design and component-first UI

Treat the web UI as a hierarchy of parts and a cohesive whole at the same time. Do not dump a screen into a route file. Build and reuse components, then compose them into templates and pages.

Styling is not this rule. Follow the Mantine rule first: use `@mantine/core` when a component exists. Colocate a `.module.css` only when layout still needs it, and follow the CSS Modules rule for tokens, layers, and `composes`.

Atomic Design is not a waterfall. Do not invent every button in isolation, then hope a page appears. Zoom into a component, then step back to the page. Parts inform the whole; the whole informs the parts.

## Layers

| Layer | Owns | Does not own |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Atom | One HTML control or styled wrapper: button, input, label, heading, icon | Other app components, data fetching, page layout |
| Molecule | A small group of atoms with one job: labeled field, search form | Section-level layout, route data |
| Organism | A distinct section: header, plant list, garden card grid | Route loaders, URL params |
| Template | Page skeleton and slots (`children` or named regions) | Fetching, domain records, real copy |
| Page | React Router route module: loaders/actions, real data, wiring a template | New atoms invented inline |

When unsure, go **one level lower** and compose up.

## Folder tree

Put reusable UI under `apps/web/app/components/`. Route modules stay pages.

```
apps/web/app/
  components/
    atoms/
    molecules/
    organisms/
    templates/
  routes/
    gardens.tsx   # SPA island page
    my-garden.tsx # MPA page
  root.tsx        # document shell, not a template
  routes.tsx      # route table, not UI
```

One component per folder: `Button.tsx`, plus `Button.module.css` only when the wrapper needs layout CSS. Name folders and files after the component, not the screen (`SearchField`, not `HomeSearch`).

`root.tsx` is the HTML document. `routes.tsx` only registers routes. Neither is a template or a page UI.

## Dependency direction

Composition flows one way. Never reverse:

```
pages → templates → organisms → molecules → atoms
```

- Lower layers never import higher layers.
- Atoms never import other app components.
- Organisms may import other organisms.
- Templates import organisms (and below), never pages.
- Pages import templates (and below). Keep pages thin.
- Data fetching lives in **pages**. Follow the web routing and data-fetching rules (`/gardens` uses `useQuery`; `/my-garden` is a static stub). Organisms may receive data as props. Never `useQuery`/`useMutation` or `fetch` in atoms, molecules, or templates.
- Do not import another component's `.module.css`.

## Component-first workflow

On any new screen or UI change:

1. **Inventory** — list the UI pieces before writing a route.
2. **Reuse** — search `@mantine/core`, then `app/components/`. Do not invent Button, Title, Text, Anchor, Stack, Group, Card, Alert, Loader, or TextInput atoms.
3. **Classify** — place each new piece at the lowest honest layer.
4. **Build** — create missing atoms → molecules → organisms → template, then wire the page. Atoms that wrap Mantine stay thin (map props, render the Mantine component).
5. **Check the whole** — compose them in the route. Verify the page, including the browser for visual work.
6. **Extract on growth** — if a route or organism grows past one job, split it down a level.

Route files compose templates and organisms. They do not invent new atoms as inline markup.

## Agent do / don't

**Do**

- Search `@mantine/core` and existing atoms/molecules/organisms before creating new ones
- Keep route modules thin: load data, pass props, render a template
- Give components props instead of hard-coding feature copy inside atoms
- Extract a molecule when the same atom cluster appears twice
- Re-check the page after extracting so the whole still holds together

**Don't**

- Implement a feature as one large JSX tree in a route module
- Put fetch/loader/`useQuery` logic in atoms, molecules, or templates
- Import a molecule from an atom, or a page from a template
- Copy-paste a button or field instead of using Mantine or reusing the atom
- Invent Button, Title, Text, or Stack atoms that duplicate `@mantine/core`
- Argue the layer for long: pick the lower one and compose

## Good / bad

```tsx
// Good — thin atom wrapping Mantine
import { Button as MantineButton } from '@mantine/core';

const variantMap = {
  primary: 'filled',
  secondary: 'default',
} as const;

type ButtonProps = {
  variant?: 'primary' | 'secondary';
  children: React.ReactNode;
};

export function Button({ variant = 'secondary', children }: ButtonProps) {
  return (
    <MantineButton type="button" variant={variantMap[variant]}>
      {children}
    </MantineButton>
  );
}
```

```tsx
// Good — molecule composing Mantine
import { Button, TextInput } from '@mantine/core';
import styles from './SearchField.module.css';

type SearchFieldProps = {
  label: string;
  value: string;
  onChange: (value: string) => void;
  onSubmit: () => void;
};

export function SearchField({
  label,
  value,
  onChange,
  onSubmit,
}: SearchFieldProps) {
  return (
    <form
      className={styles.root}
      onSubmit={(event) => {
        event.preventDefault();
        onSubmit();
      }}
    >
      <TextInput
        label={label}
        value={value}
        onChange={(event) => onChange(event.currentTarget.value)}
      />
      <Button>Search</Button>
    </form>
  );
}
```

```tsx
// Good — template is layout and slots only
import { SiteHeader } from '../organisms/SiteHeader/SiteHeader';
import styles from './AppShell.module.css';

type AppShellProps = {
  children: React.ReactNode;
};

export function AppShell({ children }: AppShellProps) {
  return (
    <div className={styles.root}>
      <SiteHeader />
      <main className={styles.main}>{children}</main>
    </div>
  );
}
```

```tsx
export default function GardensPage() {
  return (
    <AppShell>
      <GardensPanel />
    </AppShell>
  );
}

function GardensPanel() {
  const { data, isPending, isError, refetch } = useQuery(gardensQuery());
  if (isPending) return <p>Loading gardens…</p>;
  if (isError) return <Button onClick={() => refetch()}>Retry</Button>;
  return <GardenList gardens={data} />;
}
```

```tsx
export default function MyGardenPage() {
  return (
    <AppShell>
      <Text>this has yet to be implemented :(</Text>
    </AppShell>
